  ggen:outputContract "A receipt JSON that, per commit 3b294a8ce's own doc comment on the new `schema` field, \"deserializes as v1\" when the field is absent -- i.e. every pre-3b294a8ce receipt on disk is implicitly schema v1 with no itemized admission ledger, no standing_ceiling lattice, no closed 8-class equivalence map, no post-admission obligation_count -- all of which schema v2's ReceiptEpochV2 payload (crates/praxis-core/src/receipt_epoch.rs) adds" ;
  ggen:errorContract "Same ReceiptRecord error handling as today (schema is descriptive only, per the field's own doc comment: \"Not part of the chain-hash computation\")" ;
  ggen:sideEffects "Prior to 3b294a8ce, every hardcoded `Green` andon-status write site wrote directly; commit 3b294a8ce's message describes v2 as replacing every hardcoded Green write site with a derived andon computed from the v2 ledger -- a real behavior change, not just an added optional field" ;
  ggen:orderingRequirements "v1 receipts remain readable (\"dual-read/single-write compatibility\" per the commit message) -- v2 is additive, not a breaking cutover" ;
  ggen:defaultBehavior "`#[serde(default = \"crate::receipt_epoch::default_schema\")]` on the `schema` field means old receipts silently deserialize with schema=SCHEMA_V1 and v2=None rather than failing to parse" ;
